w is  trying to do with this other than show  that ellen is trying to do good in her  position of power but is coming up  against resistance  after the meeting larry senses that  she's stressed so he makes the  suggestion that they go to visit jsc  which she hasn't been to since she won  the election when she arrives there's  more protesters outside and you see that  jimmy stevens is in the crowd he brought  up problems he had with nasa at danny's  wedding so i guess it makes sense for  him to be at this protest where he gets  recognized by a reporter and then a girl  named sunny comes up to introduce  herself and invite him to have beers  with her and her friends afterwards when  they get together you see that her  boyfriend is the moon marine pilot that  tracy was training to fly the l-sam in  season 2. he doesn't believe that the  government is telling the real story of  what happened on the moon which we know  is true but him and his friends have  twisted things around to fit a different  narrative  where rather than covering up a second  reactor this is all about dividing the  moon to split up the helium-3 and there  are some interesting things going on in  this part of the story but it does feel  a little out of place so i'm not sure  how i feel about what's going on here in  space there's a little montage of life  on sojourner and phoenix to give an idea  of what the trip is like things look a  lot more comfortable on the ladder we  even see ed jogging around thanks to the  spin gravity but we do see that morale  is high under danielle's command even if  it is just the quiet before the storm on  phoenix the crew are drinking brews and  messing around and the lioness who  showed tracy jamestown for the first  time when she first arrived is acting  out a scene from the movie about tracy  and gordo when danny walks in this leads  to a confrontation where he sort of  pushes him around and pressures him into  doing this other scene from the movie  which is uncomfortable for everyone and  then ed shows up to break it up he  stresses that he needs danny to lead by  example after all this is the reason  that he wanted to bring him in the first  place to straighten him out to give him  a purpose and he'll need him to control  his temper to do that which all feels  like foreshadowing for something bad  that'll happen before the trip is over  at jsc ellen enters mission control and  gets her photo op in a standing ovation  she doesn't have to pretend to be  thrilled to be back it's clear that it  makes her emotional margot sort of pulls  elena aside and says it never changes  the people at nasa do all the hard work  but the politicians grab the glory when  elena points out that ellen's one of  them margot is quick to warn her that  she's not anymore ellen gives a moving  speech about how they pulled things  together how they worked as a team to  beat helios and when she thanks them for  their service to their country you see  margot drop her head with the tinge of  shame and this along with a lot of other  hints confirmed that she did have to  help the soviets with their nuclear  engine that engine will be the catalyst  for the episode ending crisis on  sojourner kelly gets a call from a  cosmonaut on mars 94. he warns her that  his commanders are going to do something  very dangerous to try to win the race  and before he can get into the details  he has to get off the call and then you  see them fire up those nuclear engines  they have a plan that would get them  there three days ahead of everyone else  but when their burn doesn't last long  enough it's obvious that they have a  major malfunction  danielle tells ed that their engines are  in meltdown and there's only 72 hours to  make a rescue attempt neither of the  ships have enough fuel to do the rescue  and still make mars orbit so it means  that going after them is also a ticket  home ed realizes that it makes the most  sense for phoenix to do it and is  willing to sacrifice his chance at glory  only when he explains this to helios  mission control everyone who had a  history with nasa is all for it while  deb and his faithful vote to keep going  and let nasa deal with the rescue there  are two flashes here you can't miss  initially danny isn't behind ed's plan  and on the ground karen is starting to  have second thoughts about dev's  motivations and i mentioned in my last  video that in future seasons it was  getting hard to imagine who would be  left at nasa but after seeing this that  extra money might not be as much of an  incentive  when ed finds out what they decided he  decides not to change anything he's  gonna go ahead with the rescue mission  but he finds out that when they sent the  last message they also sent a software  update that locked them out of the  controls dev anticipated that ed  wouldn't follow the order so he took  over the ship and now it's essentially  flying on autopilot the news gets around  and i love that margot suggested  nationalizing his company but in the end  nasa decides to do what needs done they  throw away their mission to mars and set  out to save the cosmonauts lives on the  approach danny tells her crew that the  soviet ship uses the same fuel as  sojourner and asks one of her crew to go  and film the ship to see if houston can  figure out a way to transfer the fuel  over of course when they bring the  cosmonauts over things start to go wrong  elena and margot notice a problem on  earth but because of the time that it  takes a message to get from them to the  crew they aren't able to warn them mars  94 ends up crashing into sojourner two  astronauts and one cosmonaut are killed  and the episode ends with everything up  in the air  there's a lot of interesting things  going on dev's decision changed the  nature of the race and the mars 94  situation sets up the probability of a  joint mission between nasa and the  soviets there is some built-in tension  and having the defector on board doesn't  